<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tezozomoc</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1426</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tezozomoc was the long-reigning ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanec</a> state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azcapotzalco">Azcapotzalco</a>, which dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a> in the late fourteenth and early fifteenth centuries. He died in 1426. His death triggered a succession struggle, during which his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maxtla">Maxtla</a> allegedly had the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chimalpopoca">Chimalpopoca</a> murdered, setting off the war that founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>.</p></div>
